{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,4]],"date-time":"2026-09-04T20:41:24Z","timestamp":1788554484962,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":83,"publisher":"EDP Sciences","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,28]],"date-time":"2024-10-28T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1730073600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001732","name":"Danmarks Grundforskningsfond","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["DNRF140"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["DNRF140"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001732","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100020884","name":"Agencia Nacional de Investigaci\u00f3n y Desarrollo","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["FB210003"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["FB210003"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100020884","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["A&amp;A"],"accepted":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,18]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,11]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>JWST has revealed a class of numerous, extremely compact sources with rest-frame red optical\/near-infrared (NIR) and blue ultraviolet (UV) colours nicknamed \u2018little red dots\u2019. We present one of the highest signal-to-noise ratio JWST NIRSpec prism spectra of a little red dot, J0647_1045 at <jats:italic>z<\/jats:italic>\u2004=\u20044.5319\u2005\u00b1\u20050.0001, and examine its NIRCam morphology to differentiate the origin of the UV and optical\/NIR emission and elucidate the nature of the little red dot phenomenon. J0647_1045 is unresolved (<jats:italic>r<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>e<\/jats:sub>\u2004\u2272\u20040.17 kpc) in the three NIRCam long-wavelength filters but significantly extended (<jats:italic>r<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>e<\/jats:sub>\u2004=\u20040.45\u2005\u00b1\u20050.06 kpc) in the three short-wavelength filters, indicating a red compact source in a blue star-forming galaxy. The spectral continuum shows a clear change in slope, from blue in the optical\/UV to red in the rest-frame optical\/NIR, which is consistent with two distinct components fit by power laws with different attenuations: <jats:italic>A<\/jats:italic><jats:sub><jats:italic>V<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sub>\u2004=\u20040.38\u2005\u00b1\u20050.01 (UV) and <jats:italic>A<\/jats:italic><jats:sub><jats:italic>V<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sub>\u2004=\u20045.61\u2005\u00b1\u20050.04 (optical\/NIR). Fitting the H<jats:italic>\u03b1<\/jats:italic> line requires both broad (full width at half maximum of \u223c4300\u2005\u00b1\u2005100 km s<jats:sup>\u22121<\/jats:sup>) and narrow components, but none of the other emission lines, including H<jats:italic>\u03b2<\/jats:italic>, show evidence of broadness. We calculated <jats:italic>A<\/jats:italic><jats:sub><jats:italic>V<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sub>\u2004=\u20040.9\u2005\u00b1\u20050.4 from the Balmer decrement using narrow H<jats:italic>\u03b1<\/jats:italic> and H<jats:italic>\u03b2<\/jats:italic> and <jats:italic>A<\/jats:italic><jats:sub><jats:italic>V<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sub>\u2004&gt;\u20044.1\u2005\u00b1\u20050.1 from broad H<jats:italic>\u03b1<\/jats:italic> and an upper limit on broad H<jats:italic>\u03b2<\/jats:italic>, which is consistent with blue and red continuum attenuation, respectively. Based on a single-epoch H<jats:italic>\u03b1<\/jats:italic> line width, the mass of the central black hole is 8<jats:sub>\u22120.4<\/jats:sub><jats:sup>+0.5<\/jats:sup>\u2005\u00d7\u200510<jats:sup>8<\/jats:sup> M<jats:sub>\u2299<\/jats:sub>. Our findings are consistent with a multi-component model, in which the optical\/NIR and broad lines arise from a highly obscured, spatially unresolved region, likely a relatively massive active galactic nucleus, while the less obscured UV continuum and narrow lines arise, at least partly, from a small but spatially resolved star-forming host galaxy.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1051\/0004-6361\/202348857","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,27]],"date-time":"2024-09-27T18:43:59Z","timestamp":1727462639000},"page":"A52","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":103,"title":["Deciphering the JWST spectrum of a \u2018little red dot\u2019 at <i>z<\/i> \u223c 4.53: An obscured AGN and its star-forming host"],"prefix":"10.1051","volume":"691","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5289-3291","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Meghana","family":"Killi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4465-8264","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Darach","family":"Watson","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2680-005X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Gabriel","family":"Brammer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0639-025X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Conor","family":"McPartland","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0243-6575","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jacqueline","family":"Antwi-Danso","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Rosa","family":"Newshore","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Dan","family":"Coe","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Natalie","family":"Allen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8149-8298","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Johan P. U.","